                    <fr:title text="CSS (cheapest, most flexible)">CSS (cheapest, most flexible)</fr:title>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>Anything visual — fonts, colors, spacing, max-widths, column behavior, sticky sidebars, link styling, code block treatment — is a <html:code>theme/style.css</html:code> edit. A new theme like <html:code>themes/dracula.css</html:code> demonstrates the pattern: scope rules under a class injected by <html:code><![CDATA[\meta{theme}{name}]]></html:code> so multiple themes can coexist. Capucci's narrower main column, prominent serif body, and quiet metadata are almost certainly all CSS.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
