                    </fr:date>
                    <fr:source-path>/Users/stevenschaefer/forest/trees/sss-0099.tree</fr:source-path>
                    <fr:title text="Fonts">Fonts</fr:title>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>Add <html:code>.woff2</html:code> files under <html:code>theme/fonts/</html:code> and declare them via <html:code>@font-face</html:code> in <html:code>style.css</html:code>, then update the body <html:code>font-family</html:code> stack. Replacing Inria Sans with a serif (e.g. EB Garamond, Crimson Pro, Equity, Concourse) or a more distinctive sans (Inter Display, Fraunces) is a one-file edit. KaTeX fonts are independent and should be left alone.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
