                    <fr:title text="Per-tree layouts via metadata">Per-tree layouts via metadata</fr:title>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p><html:code><![CDATA[\meta{layout}{wide|dashboard|table|kanban}]]></html:code> and <html:code><![CDATA[\meta{theme}{dracula|...}]]></html:code> inject CSS classes (see the compiler's <html:code>Htmx_client.ml</html:code>) that you can target from <html:code>style.css</html:code>. New layouts cost nothing on the OCaml side — pick a name, add the class hook, write the CSS. The home page already exploits this with <html:code>layout-wide</html:code>.</html:p>
