                    <fr:title text="Home page composition">Home page composition</fr:title>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>The home page is just a tree (<html:code>trees/public/index.tree</html:code>) — its structure is fully under your control via <html:code><![CDATA[\transclude]]></html:code>, <html:code><![CDATA[\grid]]></html:code>/<html:code><![CDATA[\col]]></html:code>, and per-tree metadata. Capucci-style "front of forest" layouts (a short bio, a hand-curated featured-trees list, a recent-activity column) are achievable today by editing <html:code>index.tree</html:code> and writing a couple of CSS rules; no compiler change needed.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
                </fr:tree>
