                    <fr:title text="XSL templates (medium cost)">XSL templates (medium cost)</fr:title>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>Structural changes — moving the TOC, suppressing metadata blocks, restructuring the article header, changing how transclusions are wrapped — live in <html:code>theme/tree.xsl</html:code> (~490 lines) and friends. Editable in-place, but easy to break, and changes drift from upstream on every <html:code>theme/</html:code> submodule update. Reserve for things CSS genuinely cannot do.</html:p>
                  </fr:mainmatter>
