                <fr:title text="Capucci-inspired ideas worth trying">Capucci-inspired ideas worth trying</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:ul><html:li><html:strong>Narrower body column with a serif.</html:strong> A 60–70ch <html:code>max-width</html:code> on the article column, paired with a serif body font, is the single biggest visual shift and is pure CSS.</html:li>
<html:li><html:strong>Quieter metadata.</html:strong> Default Forester surfaces tree IDs, dates, taxons fairly prominently; Capucci tucks them away. <html:code><![CDATA[.metadata { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--muted) }]]></html:code> territory.</html:li>
<html:li><html:strong>Restructured home page.</html:strong> Replace the current bio + transclusion stack with a hand-curated front matter (recent writing, ongoing projects, a "what I'm reading" block) — pure <html:code>index.tree</html:code> edit.</html:li>
<html:li><html:strong>Sectioned sidebar nav.</html:strong> A persistent left rail listing top-level topics. Achievable with a new <html:code><![CDATA[\meta{layout}{...}]]></html:code> that adds a sidebar slot, then CSS grid for placement.</html:li></html:ul>
              </fr:mainmatter>
