                <fr:title text="Open questions">Open questions</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:ul><html:li>Should new themes be shipped as switchable overlays (<html:code><![CDATA[\meta{theme}{name}]]></html:code>, like Dracula today) or as a single replaced base style? Overlays let you A/B variants per tree but balloon CSS quickly.</html:li>
<html:li>How much should diverge from the upstream base theme before maintenance pain (submodule conflicts on <html:code>theme/</html:code>) outweighs the visual gain? Vendoring <html:code>theme/</html:code> fully is one answer.</html:li>
<html:li>Do any of the desired layout changes actually require XSL edits, or is CSS grid + class hooks sufficient? Worth prototyping the Capucci home-page rework in pure CSS first to find out.</html:li></html:ul>
              </fr:mainmatter>
